card.statement:
Let $\varepsilon\in\mathbb R$,
$0<\varepsilon <1/3$, and let the
sequence of real numbers

\begin{equation}
\delta_1,\
\tau_1,\
\delta_2,\
\tau_2,\
\delta_3,\
\tau_3,\ \dots
\end{equation}

be defined by induction:

\begin{equation*}
\delta_1=\tau_1=\varepsilon^5,\qquad
\delta_{i+1}
=\varepsilon^{-1}\delta_i\tau _i,\qquad
\tau_{i+1}=\tau_i
+\varepsilon^{-1}\delta_i.
\end{equation*}

Then

\begin{equation}
0<\delta_{i}<
\varepsilon ^{2i},\qquad
0<\tau_i<\varepsilon ^{3}\qquad\text{for all
$i=1,2,\dots$}
\end{equation}
